    A never-fired cron is NOT automatically a fault: a monthly cron added
    after its day-of-month, or a workflow added today, has legitimately not
    reached a slot. The cron and the age are printed so that is decidable
    here rather than inferred from a count. NEVER_FIRED_GRACE_DAYS=40.

    COVERAGE: 4 repos, 509 workflows, 509 active, 101 JUDGED
    (>= 3 completed scheduled runs each). NOT judged: 407 with no
    schedule: block — their failures surface on the commit that caused them —
    and 1 that declare a cron but have never produced a run,
    named above rather than counted. A workflow is judged on its last 3
    scheduled runs whenever they happened, so a firing delay cannot skew it.
    DEAD means none of those 3 runs worked: each failed, was skipped, or never
    started (startup_failure). A window holding anything else — a success, or
    cancelled, timed_out, action_required, neutral — is counted healthy above.
